Falsifies `jh7110_clock_and_reset::verification::is_deasserted_reads_the_bit_the_mask_names`.

The defect: the sense of the test is inverted, so a line still in reset reads as released and a
released one as held. A driver would wait forever on a device that came up correctly, or proceed
against one still in reset.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, equality with the named status bit.

diff --git a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
index e840194c9..4d3b8c5a8 100644
--- a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
@@ -1228,7 +1228,7 @@
 /// Name: ratified 2026-10-26 (UTC).
 #[must_use]
 pub const fn is_deasserted(status_word: u32, mask: u32) -> bool {
-    status_word & mask != 0
+    status_word & mask == 0
 }
 
